{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["PWM_S1G2", "U19", "U7"],
      "pins": ["PWM_S1G2.6", "U19.1", "U7.11"],
      "nets": ["NET0100", "NET0108"],
      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet the 6th signal pin of the servo header PWM_S1G2 is wired to NET0100, which is the Winbond NAND flash chip-select net (U19 pin 1 CS, also driven by FCC MCU pin PA4). The PCA9685 LED5 output (U7 pin 11) is NET0108, and NET0108 does not appear anywhere on the servo header. The header's 8 signal nets are {NET0022,NET0091,NET0173,NET0116,NET0144,NET0100,NET0047,NET0124} whereas the PCA9685 LED0-LED7 nets are {NET0022,NET0091,NET0173,NET0116,NET0144,NET0108,NET0047,NET0124} — i.e. LED5 (NET0108) is dropped from the header and flash CS (NET0100) is inserted in its place.",
      "expected": "The 16-channel PWM driver's eight used outputs LED0-LED7 (U7 pins 6-13) must map one-to-one to the eight servo header signal pins, so header pin 6 should carry LED5 = NET0108. The SPI flash chip-select (NET0100) is a separate MCU-controlled signal and must not be merged with a servo PWM line.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: PWM_S1G2 left column rows 1-8 = NET0022, NET0091, NET0173, NET0116, NET0144, NET0100, NET0047, NET0124"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U7 PCA9685PW pin 11 LED5 = NET0108; U19 W25N01GVZEIG_TR pin 1 CS = NET0100"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM) ... 5 V feeds the servo/PWM connector bank (via PCA9685PW)"}
      ],
      "impact": "Servo header channel 6 is shorted to the SPI flash CS line: every MCU flash access pulses that header pin (a servo would twitch or be driven with non-PWM levels), and a servo connected there loads/disturbs the flash CS net, risking corrupted NAND reads/writes. Meanwhile the intended 6th PWM output (LED5/NET0108) is left unconnected, so that servo channel produces no signal.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the board matches the specification (correct MIC26903/LD39200 power stage, INA219 at 0x40 with a 10 mΩ shunt, dual STM32H753/STM32F405 MCUs, BMI088/IIS2MDCTR/MPRLS sensor set, and the documented barometer reset/interrupt pin swap). The one drawing-supported deviation is on the FCC Peripherals sheet: servo header pin 6 is wired to the flash chip-select net NET0100 instead of the PCA9685 LED5 output NET0108, bridging the SPI flash CS line to a servo PWM header and leaving LED5 open."
}

